The function $P$ is translation invariant, depends only on the convex hull, and is Lipschitz for Hausdorff distance. The function $$p(w)=P([0,w])$$ is a polyhedral norm on $W$. The group $$\label{eq:support-symmetry-group}
 \mathcal A=\{A\in\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}(W):P(AE)=P(E)\text{ for every nonempty
 compact convex }E\subset W\}$$ is finite. Its pullback action permutes the oriented rays of the generator weights $\alpha_i$.

Suppose their joint law $\nu_r$ gives full measure to a Borel admissible domain $\Theta_r\subset[-R_r,R_r]^a$, is absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure, and satisfies $$1\le R_r\le e^{o(r)},\qquad
 \frac{d\nu_r}{d\theta}\le e^{o(r)}
       \quad\text{almost everywhere}.$$

Suppose that, for every segment $J=\{z\exp_\infty(tv):0\le t\le T\}\Subset\mathcal U_\delta$, $T>0$, both $$\label{eq:affinity-two-inequalities}
 \frac{f(z\exp_\infty(Tv))-f(z)}{T}
       \in\operatorname{conv}(\mathcal A\pi v),
 \qquad P(f(J))\ge T p(\pi v)$$ hold.

For each source and target ray pair in Lemma <a href="#lem:ray-boundaries" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:ray-boundaries">45</a>, there is a fixed compact ball $U\subset L_\alpha$ with nonempty interior such that $$\label{eq:boundary-volume}
 \mathop{\mathrm{vol}}_{L_\beta}\bigl(f_\beta(x\cdot U)\bigr)
 \asymp e^{\ell_\beta(\pi F(x))}
 \qquad(x\in G).$$ The comparison constants and the choices of balls are uniform over the fixed quasi-isometry family.

